`{ATLAS_GITHUB_APP_SLUG}[bot]`. Another App's bot does not count. **Retries.** A failed review posts nothing. A failed post is tried at most five times. The waits before the later tries are 5, 15, 30, and 60 seconds, each stretched by up to 20%. The fifth attempt does not wait. A 429 waits. A 403 waits only when `Retry-After` is present, or `x-ratelimit-remaining` is 0 and `x-ratelimit-reset` is present, or the body says it is a secondary rate limit. A secondary limit waits at least 60 seconds. A wait above 15 minutes is cut to 15 minutes. A 401, a 403 that is not one of those cases, and a 422 are not retried. Each attempt's deadline is 45 seconds and includes the token mint. **Cost.** No standing Machine is created here. The model spend stays inside the caps D25 and the agentic loop already enforce. The extra cost is one GitHub write of a COMMENT. The always-on Machine's price is D53's, about $6.70 per 30 days plus the volume, and it is not spent by merging this PR. **Reversibility.** Stop the process or disable the webhook. A COMMENT already accepted by GitHub stays; that request cannot be recalled. The one-off CLI and D37's app are unchanged. There is no schema migration. **Revisit** after the first live webhook review, or if COMMENT-only is dropped. Tests use fakes. Nothing was posted to GitHub from this change.
 
